{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-i-as-braiding-orientation","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:i-as-braiding-orientation","kind":"remark","title":"The imaginary unit $i$ as braiding-orientation datum","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/sec-linearisation-convention","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-laplace-fourier-wick-rotation","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-braiding-induced-ordering"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-braiding-induced-ordering","tags":["braiding","orientation","imaginary-unit","wick-rotation","cr-structure","arrow-of-time","cpt-symmetry"],"text":"i-as-braiding-orientation.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:i-as-braiding-orientation\"></a><p>The imaginary unit <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">i</code> serves as the orientation of the braiding <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">c_{V,V}</code> versus <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">c_{V,V}^{-1}</code>.</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Wick rotation</strong>: The rotation <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">t \\mapsto it</code> converting the Laplace half-plane to the Fourier half-plane flips upon <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">i \\mapsto -i</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>CR complex structure</strong>: The operator <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">J \\colon H \\to H</code> secures the CR orientation.</li>\n<li><strong>Arrow of time</strong>: The positive crossing <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">c_{V,V}</code> defines forward time in the Hecke basis ordering, while <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">c_{V,V}^{-1}</code> reverses it. Negating <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">i</code> equates to flipping the crossing orientation.</li>\n</ol>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/i-as-braiding-orientation.md","heading":"Remark","number":"3.24.4"}
